Subject: [PATCH 277/280] WIP: clk: rockchip: rk3399: add PLL rates for the
 1000/1001 HDMI clocks

The PLL rate table has the integer HDMI pixel clocks but none of their
1000/1001 variants. VPLL rounds a request down to the next table rate,
so 148.352 MHz becomes 106.5 MHz, and the dw-hdmi glue rejects the mode
because that is more than 0.1% away. Every 59.94, 29.97 and 23.976 Hz
mode is removed.

Add fractional entries at the rates DRM uses for these modes: 593.407,
296.703, 148.352 and 74.176 MHz. Run the VCO at 2967 MHz (3115 MHz for
74.176 MHz) as the vendor kernel does, with the fraction chosen so that
the rate calculated from the registers equals the table rate. A higher
rate makes a child divider round up to divide by 2, and any difference
makes the clk core predict a different rate than it later reads back,
which leaves the dclk_vop0 fractional mux selected by its notifier.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Christian Hewitt <christianshewitt@gmail.com>
